{"id": "EUVD-2026-108136", "enisaUuid": "0f161def-89bd-362d-99df-d6ffa3ff06e3", "description": "Lotus through 0.10.2 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability in ChangeUserOrganizationView.post that allows authenticated users to join any organization by supplying its UUID. Self-registered attackers who know another organization's UUID can send a POST request to /app/switch_organization/ to access that tenant's data and billing configuration.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:50", "baseScore": 7.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/BkUc3WL2Mx", "https://github.com/uselotus/lotus/blob/0.10.2/backend/metering_billing/views/views.py#L326-L340", "https://github.com/uselotus/lotus", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/lotus-through-0.10.2-authorization-bypass-via-switch-organization-endpoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5pvq-7p6f-h4j3", "CVE-2026-115334"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6c3d7cf3-bbe5-3b43-a37e-7ee72a1b58ac", "product": {"name": "lotus", "vendor": {"name": "filecoin-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.10.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "57f361fc-f8ce-3585-a0c3-acecc19929eb", "vendor": {"name": "uselotus"}}], "isExploited": false}